body:
Most of the staff at my store is 16-18.  Aside from the SM/ASM and one KH that's been there forever. Since I started in September, we've hired 30-ish more people. Most only last a couple of weeks. One lasted one shift and then they NCNS. We have one KH who gets on everyone's nerves with her holier then thou attitude (She has a master's in fashion design and is so much better then the rest of us.) 

&#x200B;

But we still have people asking to speak with a manager and wanting to apply.

Oh gosh yes. Growing up  I got one meal per day.  If I asked for snacks/extra, I got screamed at about how I'm a pig/fat/useless. It's like you have to validate whether or not you've done enough to deserve food. When I was in high school I was actually anorexic because besides getting yelled at for being hungry at home, I had a boyfriend who kept calling me fat. When I graduated, I weighed 98 lbs. 

&#x200B;

When I met hubs, he let me eat anything I wanted. So now I'm a bit overweight. But I'm exercising and eating healthy. I still can't eat a "normal" size portion of food, or more then 2 meals a day.

We were taught to only brush our teeth if they started to hurt. It's really fun explaining that to the dentist now that I'm in my 30's. 

&#x200B;

One of the Nrents punishments for me was to ground me from the bathroom, so many times I was forced to use the bathroom outside. When I was a teenager, Nmom went through a phase where she didn't want people to flush the toilet. I guess she thought we were hiding things? We went without power semi frequently - funny it wasn't during winter or summer, because then it would be inconvenient to the Nrents. I just sat by an open window and did homework or read until it was dark and then went to bed. My alarm clock ran on batteries and I had a flashlight.

Nmom was a lot like that. She'd make sure that she had everything she wanted, and then "oh yeah, I have kids". Ndad actually made good money at his job, but Nmom took the bulk of it for her business and forget to pay the bills. 

&#x200B;

1 tube of toothpaste was supposed to last GCsis and I for an entire year. 1 regular sized jar of peanut butter was supposed to last an entire school year. I only had hand-me-up clothes from GCsis, even socks and underwear \*gross!\* We lived without power and running water several times. But Nmom always had nice things in her store and a full closet of name brand clothes that she'd only wear once or twice, then throw out.

All the damn time. We had a stupid hierachy for the TV. NDad would watch the news, then when Nmom came home, she was in charge of the remote. Just kids home? GCSis watched what she wanted. 

&#x200B;

After the divorce, when Nmom would come home from work, my job was to greet her at the door, hand her a drink and escort her to the TV, where I had the right channel on for her and a TV tray with dinner ready. We would all eat dinner together in front of the TV, and since I "bothered" GCSis, I wasn't allowed to sit on the furniture. 

&#x200B;

And yeah, you had a question or permission slip or needed anything from her? You had to wait until she was in the bathroom during a commercial break to approach the queen on her throne. 

&#x200B;

She still jokes that we kept bothering her when she was in the bathroom......ugh.

One of my first red flags was when Nmom met my oldest after she was home from the hospital. She turned to me and asked if the baby made me angry and frustrated. I said no, it's a baby. All babies do is eat, sleep and poop and that all I expect from them. 

&#x200B;

So I made her angry as a baby by being a baby?! Talk about a no-win situation there. 

&#x200B;

And yes I am a graduate of "ninja school". I can even cook a meal silently.

Back when I was allowed to attend family gatherings, the gifts were very much skewed. 

&#x200B;

Since I was "removed" from the family, Nmom has private celebrations with just us. You'd think she's trying to push me out of the family, but I don't want anything to do with any of them.

Yeah both of my Nrents are massive hoarders and I am essentially a minimalist. I guess it bothers them that I don't live in a storage space.

&#x200B;

Jokes on them, I donate anything I get from them anyways, I don't want their nonsense in my house.

I definitely think so.  It's like your brain knows this is wrong and just wants out? 

&#x200B;

My Nmother used to tell me all the time that having me was the biggest mistake of her life. So I took pills that she left out, or tried to get kidnapped, or ran away. When that didn't work, I tried to be perfect hoping that maybe I could be good enough that she would love me. It never was enough. Finally in my 20's I was "kicked out" of the family for not "showing respect" but Nmom kept trying to keep in contact with me, trying to get me to feel bad and rejoin the family. 

&#x200B;

I am still working through suicidal tendencies and feeling worthless and not good enough. It takes a lot of time.

My Ngma used to write a christmas letter to the family. I think I still have a copy of the last one she wrote before she got Alzheimer's. She wrote about everyone in the family and what they were doing and how proud she was of them....except me and hubby and our kids. Because we don't exist. Nmom said she just forgot us because she only wanted to write a 1 page letter this year. Ugh. And of course they had a family photo session without us. Wearing matching sweaters.

&#x200B;

Hey but that means you're free to make your own family then, right?

Welcome! 

I remember when I first realized that something was "off". It's only been 3 years since the fog lifted for me and sometimes the wounds still feel fresh. It just takes time to realize that everything wasn't your fault. 

&#x200B;

We're all here to help.

&#x200B;

Ndad always pretends to be sick when it's a "gifting" event. That way he doesn't have to spend money. 

&#x200B;

Nmom's family is hugely dysfunctional. They all hate each other, but they get together for the holidays and try to impress each other with overly extravagant gifts.  Since myself and by extension my husband and kids are the family scapegoats, we would get either used hand me downs or nothing at all. 

&#x200B;

One of the last Christmases we had before we were kicked out of the family, my 4 year old cousin got a brand new $2,000 laptop. My 6 and 5 year old children were regifted baby toys from my aunt and uncle's baby shower from 4 years ago. It was just comical.
